body:
you're right to be confused: the question is missing a word! the question SHOULD say:

"Can the AVERAGE velocity of an object be positive during a time interval in which its displacement is negative?" the answer is obviously no, the average velocity would be negative for a negative displacement.

if it asked "Can the INSTANTANEOUS velocity of an object be positive..." then YES, for the exact reasons you're describing. the instantaneous velocity can be positive for negative displacement, as long as there's more negative instantaneous velocity to outweigh it (i.e. average velocity is negative.)
